[2026-03-14T18:36:54.520Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JwH8PhszdegGJ8ekAM6yH8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Google Flights Clone — Test Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Page: Search Page (Home)\n     4→\n     5→### Components\n     6→- TripTypeSelector\n     7→- PassengerCountSelector\n     8→- CabinClassSelector\n     9→- AirportAutocomplete\n    10→- DatePicker\n    11→- SearchButton\n    12→- RecentSearches\n    13→- PopularDestinations\n    14→\n    15→### TripTypeSelector\n    16→\n    17→#### Test: TripTypeSelector displays default \"Round trip\" selection\n    18→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    19→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n    20→- **Action**: User observes the trip type selector\n    21→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"Round trip\" as the default selected option. It is rendered as a custom dropdown (not a native select element).\n    22→\n    23→#### Test: TripTypeSelector opens dropdown and shows all options\n    24→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    25→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, trip type selector is closed\n    26→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector\n    27→- **Expected**: A dropdown menu opens showing three options: \"Round trip\", \"One way\", and \"Multi-city\". Each option is clickable.\n    28→\n    29→#### Test: TripTypeSelector selects \"One way\" and hides return date\n    30→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector, DatePicker\n    31→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with \"Round trip\" selected, return date picker is visible\n    32→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"One way\"\n    33→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"One way\". The return date picker is hidden. The dropdown closes.\n    34→\n    35→#### Test: TripTypeSelector selects \"Multi-city\" option\n    36→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    37→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with \"Round trip\" selected\n    38→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"Multi-city\"\n    39→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"Multi-city\". The search form adjusts to support multi-city input (multiple origin/destination pairs).\n    40→\n    41→#### Test: TripTypeSelector switches back to \"Round trip\" from \"One way\"\n    42→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector, DatePicker\n    43→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" is currently selected, return date picker is hidden\n    44→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"Round trip\"\n    45→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"Round trip\". The return date picker becomes visible again.\n    46→\n    47→#### Test: TripTypeSelector closes dropdown when clicking outside\n    48→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    49→- **Initial state**: Trip type dropdown is open\n    50→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n    51→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the selection.\n    52→\n    53→#### Test: TripTypeSelector can be used multiple times in sequence\n    54→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    55→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with default \"Round trip\"\n    56→- **Action**: User selects \"One way\", then interacts with another element (e.g., clicks airport field), then opens the trip type selector again and selects \"Round trip\"\n    57→- **Expected**: Each interaction correctly updates the selector. The dropdown opens and closes properly on each use. The final state shows \"Round trip\" selected.\n    58→\n    59→### PassengerCountSelector\n    60→\n    61→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector displays default \"1 Adult\"\n    62→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    63→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n    64→- **Action**: User observes the passenger count selector\n    65→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"1\" or \"1 Adult\" as the default.\n    66→\n    67→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector opens dropdown with passenger categories\n    68→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    69→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, passenger selector is closed\n    70→- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count selector\n    71→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing three categories: Adults, Children, and Infants. Each category has a label, a current count, and \"+\" and \"−\" buttons.\n    72→\n    73→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments adult count\n    74→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    75→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n    76→- **Action**: User clicks the \"+\" button next to Adults\n    77→- **Expected**: Adults count increases to 2. The selector label updates to reflect the new total (e.g., \"2 passengers\" or \"2 Adults\").\n    78→\n    79→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector decrements adult count with minimum of 1\n    80→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    81→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n    82→- **Action**: User clicks the \"−\" button next to Adults\n    83→- **Expected**: Adults count remains at 1. The \"−\" button is disabled or has no effect since at least 1 adult is required.\n    84→\n    85→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements children\n    86→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    87→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Children count is 0\n    88→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Children twice, then clicks \"−\" once\n    89→- **Expected**: Children count goes to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n    90→\n    91→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements infants\n    92→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    93→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Infants count is 0\n    94→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n    95→- **Expected**: Infants count increases to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n    96→\n    97→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector prevents infants exceeding adults\n    98→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    99→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 1, Infants = 1\n   100→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n   101→- **Expected**: Infants count remains at 1 (cannot exceed number of adults). The \"+\" button is disabled or has no effect.\n   102→\n   103→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector closes dropdown and retains values\n   104→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n   105→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 2, Children = 1, Infants = 0\n   106→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown to close it\n   107→- **Expected**: Dropdown closes. The selector label shows the updated total (e.g., \"3 passengers\"). Reopening the dropdown shows the same values (2 Adults, 1 Child, 0 Infants).\n   108→\n   109→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector can be used repeatedly\n   110→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n   111→- **Initial state**: Search page with default passenger counts\n   112→- **Action**: User opens the selector, adds 1 adult, closes it, interacts with another element (e.g., selects cabin class), then reopens the passenger selector and adds 1 child\n   113→- **Expected**: All values persist correctly between opens. Final state shows 2 Adults, 1 Child. The selector works correctly on each subsequent use.\n   114→\n   115→### CabinClassSelector\n   116→\n   117→#### Test: CabinClassSelector displays default \"Economy\"\n   118→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   119→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n   120→- **Action**: User observes the cabin class selector\n   121→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"Economy\" as the default selected cabin class. It is rendered as a custom dropdown.\n   122→\n   123→#### Test: CabinClassSelector opens dropdown showing all cabin classes\n   124→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   125→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, cabin class selector is closed\n   126→- **Action**: User clicks the cabin class selector\n   127→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing four options: \"Economy\", \"Premium Economy\", \"Business\", and \"First\".\n   128→\n   129→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"Business\" class\n   130→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   131→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open with \"Economy\" selected\n   132→- **Action**: User clicks \"Business\"\n   133→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"Business\".\n   134→\n   135→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"Premium Economy\" class\n   136→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   137→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   138→- **Action**: User clicks \"Premium Economy\"\n   139→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"Premium Economy\".\n   140→\n   141→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"First\" class\n   142→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   143→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   144→- **Action**: User clicks \"First\"\n   145→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"First\".\n   146→\n   147→#### Test: CabinClassSelector closes dropdown when clicking outside\n   148→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   149→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   150→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n   151→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the selection.\n   152→\n   153→#### Test: CabinClassSelector can be changed multiple times\n   154→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   155→- **Initial state**: Search page with \"Economy\" selected\n   156→- **Action**: User selects \"Business\", interacts with another element, then reopens and selects \"First\", then reopens and selects \"Economy\"\n   157→- **Expected**: Each selection correctly updates the label. The final state shows \"Economy\". The dropdown works correctly on each use.\n   158→\n   159→### AirportAutocomplete\n   160→\n   161→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete origin field shows placeholder text\n   162→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   163→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with empty origin field\n   164→- **Action**: User observes the origin airport field\n   165→- **Expected**: The field displays placeholder text indicating the user should enter an origin (e.g., \"Where from?\").\n   166→\n   167→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete destination field shows placeholder text\n   168→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   169→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with empty destination field\n   170→- **Action**: User observes the destination airport field\n   171→- **Expected**: The field displays placeholder text indicating the user should enter a destination (e.g., \"Where to?\").\n   172→\n   173→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows suggestions when typing airport name\n   174→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   175→- **Initial state**: Origin field is focused and empty\n   176→- **Action**: User types \"Los Angeles\" into the origin field\n   177→- **Expected**: A suggestion dropdown appears showing matching airports, including \"Los Angeles International Airport (LAX)\". Each suggestion shows the airport name and IATA code.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows suggestions when typing IATA code\n   180→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   181→- **Initial state**: Origin field is focused and empty\n   182→- **Action**: User types \"JFK\" into the origin field\n   183→- **Expected**: A suggestion dropdown appears showing \"John F. Kennedy International Airport (JFK)\" as a match.\n   184→\n   185→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows suggestions when typing city name\n   186→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   187→- **Initial state**: Destination field is focused and empty\n   188→- **Action**: User types \"London\" into the destination field\n   189→- **Expected**: A suggestion dropdown appears showing London-area airports (e.g., \"London Heathrow (LHR)\").\n   190→\n   191→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete selects a suggestion and populates the field\n   192→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   193→- **Initial state**: User has typed \"Los\" in the origin field, suggestions are visible\n   194→- **Action**: User clicks on \"Los Angeles International Airport (LAX)\" from the suggestions\n   195→- **Expected**: The origin field is populated with the selected airport (showing name and/or code). The suggestion dropdown closes.\n   196→\n   197→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete swap button exchanges origin and destination\n   198→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   199→- **Initial state**: Origin is set to \"LAX\" and destination is set to \"JFK\"\n   200→- **Action**: User clicks the swap button between origin and destination fields","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015XqURnhAyaFzZdjoANsF8q","session_id":"e83b6a70-0e11-4c8e-bdc4-82e0f5b3de96","uuid":"9f3bb4e4-b315-4662-983c-1c010a670330"}
