[2026-03-14T18:36:56.979Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013a9UfdSAezpAZ6Ydu96m5C","type":"tool_result","content":"   200→- **Action**: User clicks the swap button between origin and destination fields\n   201→- **Expected**: Origin becomes \"JFK\" and destination becomes \"LAX\". Both fields update their displayed values.\n   202→\n   203→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete swap button works with empty fields\n   204→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   205→- **Initial state**: Origin is set to \"LAX\", destination is empty\n   206→- **Action**: User clicks the swap button\n   207→- **Expected**: Origin becomes empty, destination becomes \"LAX\".\n   208→\n   209→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete clears field and shows new suggestions\n   210→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   211→- **Initial state**: Origin field has \"LAX\" selected\n   212→- **Action**: User clears the origin field and types \"San\"\n   213→- **Expected**: The field clears the previous selection. New suggestions appear for airports matching \"San\" (e.g., \"San Francisco International Airport (SFO)\", \"San Diego International Airport (SAN)\").\n   214→\n   215→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows no results for invalid query\n   216→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   217→- **Initial state**: Origin field is focused\n   218→- **Action**: User types \"xyznonexistent\" into the origin field\n   219→- **Expected**: The suggestion dropdown shows a \"No airports found\" message or similar empty state.\n   220→\n   221→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete destination works after using origin\n   222→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   223→- **Initial state**: Origin is set to \"LAX\"\n   224→- **Action**: User clicks the destination field and types \"New York\"\n   225→- **Expected**: Suggestions appear for New York area airports. Selecting one populates the destination. Both origin and destination retain their values.\n   226→\n   227→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete can be used repeatedly\n   228→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   229→- **Initial state**: Origin and destination are both populated\n   230→- **Action**: User clears origin, types a new airport, selects it, then clears destination, types a new airport, and selects it\n   231→- **Expected**: Both fields update correctly. Autocomplete suggestions work properly on each subsequent use.\n   232→\n   233→### DatePicker\n   234→\n   235→#### Test: DatePicker departure field shows placeholder\n   236→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   237→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with no date selected\n   238→- **Action**: User observes the departure date picker\n   239→- **Expected**: The departure date field shows a placeholder (e.g., \"Departure\" or a date format hint).\n   240→\n   241→#### Test: DatePicker return field shows placeholder when Round trip\n   242→- **Components**: DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   243→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with \"Round trip\" selected\n   244→- **Action**: User observes the return date picker\n   245→- **Expected**: The return date field is visible and shows a placeholder (e.g., \"Return\" or a date format hint).\n   246→\n   247→#### Test: DatePicker opens calendar on departure field click\n   248→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   249→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, departure date field is not focused\n   250→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date field\n   251→- **Expected**: A calendar popup opens showing the current month. Past dates are disabled/grayed out. Users can navigate between months.\n   252→\n   253→#### Test: DatePicker selects a departure date\n   254→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   255→- **Initial state**: Departure date calendar is open\n   256→- **Action**: User clicks a future date (e.g., March 25)\n   257→- **Expected**: The date is selected and displayed in the departure field (e.g., \"Mar 25\" or \"2026-03-25\"). The calendar closes or shifts focus to the return date.\n   258→\n   259→#### Test: DatePicker selects a return date after departure\n   260→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   261→- **Initial state**: Departure date is set to March 25, return date calendar is open\n   262→- **Action**: User clicks a date after the departure date (e.g., April 1)\n   263→- **Expected**: The return date is set and displayed. Dates before the departure date are disabled in the return calendar.\n   264→\n   265→#### Test: DatePicker prevents selecting return date before departure\n   266→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   267→- **Initial state**: Departure date is set to March 25, return date calendar is open\n   268→- **Action**: User attempts to click March 20 (before departure)\n   269→- **Expected**: The date cannot be selected. It appears disabled/grayed out.\n   270→\n   271→#### Test: DatePicker navigates to next month\n   272→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   273→- **Initial state**: Calendar is open showing the current month\n   274→- **Action**: User clicks the \"next month\" arrow button\n   275→- **Expected**: The calendar displays the next month's dates.\n   276→\n   277→#### Test: DatePicker navigates to previous month (not before current)\n   278→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   279→- **Initial state**: Calendar is open showing the current month\n   280→- **Action**: User clicks the \"previous month\" arrow button\n   281→- **Expected**: If current month is shown, the previous button is disabled or has no effect (cannot navigate to past months). If a future month is shown, it navigates back.\n   282→\n   283→#### Test: DatePicker return field hidden when One way selected\n   284→- **Components**: DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   285→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" trip type is selected\n   286→- **Action**: User observes the date picker area\n   287→- **Expected**: Only the departure date picker is visible. The return date picker is not rendered.\n   288→\n   289→#### Test: DatePicker retains departure date when switching trip types\n   290→- **Components**: DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   291→- **Initial state**: \"Round trip\" selected with departure date March 25 and return date April 1\n   292→- **Action**: User switches to \"One way\" then back to \"Round trip\"\n   293→- **Expected**: The departure date (March 25) is retained. The return date may be cleared or retained depending on implementation.\n   294→\n   295→#### Test: DatePicker can be used repeatedly\n   296→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   297→- **Initial state**: Departure date is set to March 25\n   298→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date field again and selects a different date (e.g., March 28)\n   299→- **Expected**: The departure date updates to March 28. The calendar opens and closes correctly on subsequent uses.\n   300→\n   301→### SearchButton\n   302→\n   303→#### Test: SearchButton is displayed with prominent styling\n   304→- **Components**: SearchButton\n   305→- **Initial state**: Search page is loaded\n   306→- **Action**: User observes the search button\n   307→- **Expected**: A prominent search button is visible with the primary blue color (#1A73E8) and clear text (e.g., \"Search\" or a search icon). The button has a hover effect.\n   308→\n   309→#### Test: SearchButton navigates to results page with valid inputs\n   310→- **Components**: SearchButton, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker\n   311→- **Initial state**: Origin is \"LAX\", destination is \"JFK\", departure date is March 25, return date is April 1, trip type is \"Round trip\"\n   312→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   313→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Search Results page. The search parameters are passed to the results page. A recent search entry is saved to the database.\n   314→\n   315→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when origin is missing\n   316→- **Components**: SearchButton, AirportAutocomplete\n   317→- **Initial state**: Origin is empty, destination is \"JFK\", dates are set\n   318→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   319→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the origin field indicating it is required.\n   320→\n   321→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when destination is missing\n   322→- **Components**: SearchButton, AirportAutocomplete\n   323→- **Initial state**: Origin is \"LAX\", destination is empty, dates are set\n   324→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   325→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the destination field indicating it is required.\n   326→\n   327→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when departure date is missing\n   328→- **Components**: SearchButton, DatePicker\n   329→- **Initial state**: Origin and destination are set, departure date is empty\n   330→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   331→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the departure date field.\n   332→\n   333→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when return date is missing for round trip\n   334→- **Components**: SearchButton, DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   335→- **Initial state**: \"Round trip\" selected, origin and destination set, departure date set, return date empty\n   336→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   337→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the return date field.\n   338→\n   339→#### Test: SearchButton works for One way trip without return date\n   340→- **Components**: SearchButton, TripTypeSelector\n   341→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" selected, origin is \"LAX\", destination is \"JFK\", departure date is set\n   342→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   343→- **Expected**: The search executes successfully and navigates to the results page. No validation error for missing return date.\n   344→\n   345→#### Test: SearchButton saves search to recent searches\n   346→- **Components**: SearchButton, RecentSearches\n   347→- **Initial state**: Valid search parameters filled in, no recent searches\n   348→- **Action**: User clicks Search, then navigates back to the Search page\n   349→- **Expected**: The search appears in the recent searches section showing origin → destination, dates, and passenger count.\n   350→\n   351→### RecentSearches\n   352→\n   353→#### Test: RecentSearches shows empty state when no searches exist\n   354→- **Components**: RecentSearches\n   355→- **Initial state**: New session with no previous searches\n   356→- **Action**: User observes the area below the search form\n   357→- **Expected**: The recent searches section is either hidden or displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No recent searches\").\n   358→\n   359→#### Test: RecentSearches displays a recent search entry\n   360→- **Components**: RecentSearches\n   361→- **Initial state**: User has performed one search (LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 1 adult)\n   362→- **Action**: User navigates back to the search page and observes recent searches\n   363→- **Expected**: One recent search entry is displayed showing \"LAX → JFK\", the dates \"Mar 25 – Apr 1\", and \"1 passenger\".\n   364→\n   365→#### Test: RecentSearches clicking a recent search re-populates the form\n   366→- **Components**: RecentSearches, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker, PassengerCountSelector, TripTypeSelector, CabinClassSelector\n   367→- **Initial state**: A recent search exists (LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 2 adults, Business class, Round trip)\n   368→- **Action**: User clicks on the recent search entry\n   369→- **Expected**: The search form is populated with the recent search parameters: origin = LAX, destination = JFK, departure = Mar 25, return = Apr 1, passengers = 2 adults, cabin class = Business, trip type = Round trip. The search is executed and the app navigates to the results page.\n   370→\n   371→#### Test: RecentSearches displays multiple recent searches in order\n   372→- **Components**: RecentSearches\n   373→- **Initial state**: User has performed 3 searches in order: (1) LAX→JFK, (2) SFO→ORD, (3) LAX→LHR\n   374→- **Action**: User navigates back to the search page\n   375→- **Expected**: All three recent searches are displayed with the most recent (LAX→LHR) shown first.\n   376→\n   377→#### Test: RecentSearches updates after a new search\n   378→- **Components**: RecentSearches, SearchButton\n   379→- **Initial state**: One recent search exists (LAX → JFK)\n   380→- **Action**: User performs a new search (SFO → ORD) and returns to the search page\n   381→- **Expected**: Two recent searches are displayed. The new search (SFO → ORD) appears first, followed by the older one (LAX → JFK).\n   382→\n   383→### PopularDestinations\n   384→\n   385→#### Test: PopularDestinations grid is displayed on search page\n   386→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   387→- **Initial state**: Search page loads\n   388→- **Action**: User scrolls to see the popular destinations section below the search form\n   389→- **Expected**: A grid of destination cards is visible. Each card shows a city name, country, a colored gradient placeholder image, and a \"from $X\" starting price.\n   390→\n   391→#### Test: PopularDestinations card shows city, country, and price\n   392→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   393→- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible\n   394→- **Action**: User examines a destination card\n   395→- **Expected**: The card displays the destination city name, country name, a colored gradient image placeholder, and a starting price (e.g., \"from $199\").\n   396→\n   397→#### Test: PopularDestinations clicking a card initiates a search\n   398→- **Components**: PopularDestinations, AirportAutocomplete, SearchButton\n   399→- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible, user has no origin set\n   400→- **Action**: User clicks on a destination card (e.g., \"Tokyo, Japan\")\n   401→- **Expected**: The destination field is populated with the corresponding airport. A search is initiated to that destination (the origin may use a default or prompt the user to enter one).\n   402→\n   403→#### Test: PopularDestinations displays multiple cards in grid layout\n   404→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   405→- **Initial state**: Search page loads\n   406→- **Action**: User observes the popular destinations section\n   407→- **Expected**: Multiple destination cards are displayed in a responsive grid layout (e.g., 3-4 cards per row on desktop).\n   408→\n   409→#### Test: PopularDestinations cards have hover effect\n   410→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   411→- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible\n   412→- **Action**: User hovers over a destination card\n   413→- **Expected**: The card shows a visual hover effect (e.g., shadow increase, slight scale, or color change) indicating it is interactive/clickable.\n   414→\n   415→## Page: Search Results\n   416→\n   417→### Components\n   418→- SearchSummaryBar\n   419→- FilterSidebar\n   420→- FlightResultCard\n   421→- TrackPricesToggle\n   422→- Pagination\n   423→\n   424→### SearchSummaryBar\n   425→\n   426→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar displays search parameters after search\n   427→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   428→- **Initial state**: User searched LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 1 adult, Economy, Round trip\n   429→- **Action**: User observes the summary bar at the top of the results page\n   430→- **Expected**: The bar displays origin \"LAX\", destination \"JFK\", dates \"Mar 25 – Apr 1\", \"1 adult\", and \"Economy\" inline. Each parameter is visually distinct and clickable.\n   431→\n   432→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit origin airport\n   433→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, AirportAutocomplete\n   434→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   435→- **Action**: User clicks the origin parameter (\"LAX\") in the summary bar\n   436→- **Expected**: An inline editor opens with an airport autocomplete field pre-filled with \"LAX\". User types \"SFO\", selects \"San Francisco International Airport (SFO)\" from suggestions, and confirms. The search re-executes with SFO → JFK and results update.\n   437→\n   438→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit destination airport\n   439→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, AirportAutocomplete\n   440→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   441→- **Action**: User clicks the destination parameter (\"JFK\") in the summary bar\n   442→- **Expected**: An inline editor opens with an airport autocomplete field pre-filled with \"JFK\". User types \"ORD\", selects \"O'Hare International Airport (ORD)\" from suggestions, and confirms. The search re-executes with LAX → ORD and results update.\n   443→\n   444→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit departure date\n   445→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, DatePicker\n   446→- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with departure Mar 25\n   447→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date parameter in the summary bar\n   448→- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Mar 25 selected. User selects Mar 28. The search re-executes with the new departure date and results update.\n   449→\n   450→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit return date\n   451→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, DatePicker\n   452→- **Initial state**: Results page showing round trip search with return Apr 1\n   453→- **Action**: User clicks the return date parameter in the summary bar\n   454→- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Apr 1 selected. User selects Apr 5. The search re-executes with the new return date and results update.\n   455→\n   456→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit passengers\n   457→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, PassengerCountSelector\n   458→- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with 1 adult\n   459→- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count parameter in the summary bar\n   460→- **Expected**: A passenger selector dropdown opens showing Adults: 1, Children: 0, Infants: 0. User increments adults to 2 and closes. The search re-executes with 2 adults and results update with new pricing.\n   461→\n   462→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit cabin class\n   463→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, CabinClassSelector\n   464→- **Initial state**: Results page showing Economy search\n   465→- **Action**: User clicks the cabin class parameter in the summary bar\n   466→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First. User selects \"Business\". The search re-executes with Business class and results update with new pricing.\n   467→\n   468→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline editor closes without changes on outside click\n   469→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   470→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the origin parameter and the inline editor is open\n   471→- **Action**: User clicks outside the inline editor\n   472→- **Expected**: The inline editor closes. The original search parameters are unchanged. No re-search occurs.\n   473→\n   474→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar can be edited multiple times in sequence\n   475→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   476→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   477→- **Action**: User edits origin to SFO (results update), then edits cabin class to Business (results update again)\n   478→- **Expected**: Each edit triggers a new search. The summary bar reflects all changes: SFO → JFK, Business. Results correspond to the updated parameters.\n   479→\n   480→### FilterSidebar\n   481→\n   482→#### Test: FilterSidebar displays all filter sections\n   483→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   484→- **Initial state**: Search results page loaded with results\n   485→- **Action**: User observes the left sidebar\n   486→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays filter sections: Stops, Airlines, Price range, Duration range, Departure time, and a Sort by dropdown. All sections are visible and labeled.\n   487→\n   488→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check Nonstop\n   489→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   490→- **Initial state**: Results page with mix of nonstop and connecting flights\n   491→- **Action**: User checks the \"Nonstop\" checkbox in the Stops filter\n   492→- **Expected**: Only nonstop flights are displayed in the results list. Flights with 1+ stops are hidden.\n   493→\n   494→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check 1 stop\n   495→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   496→- **Initial state**: Results page with mix of nonstop and connecting flights, no filters applied\n   497→- **Action**: User checks the \"1 stop\" checkbox\n   498→- **Expected**: Only 1-stop flights are displayed. Nonstop and 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   499→\n   500→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check multiple options\n   501→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   502→- **Initial state**: Results page with various flights\n   503→- **Action**: User checks both \"Nonstop\" and \"1 stop\" checkboxes\n   504→- **Expected**: Both nonstop and 1-stop flights are displayed. Only 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   505→\n   506→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — uncheck to remove filter\n   507→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   508→- **Initial state**: \"Nonstop\" checkbox is checked, only nonstop flights shown\n   509→- **Action**: User unchecks \"Nonstop\"\n   510→- **Expected**: All flights are displayed again (no stops filter active).\n   511→\n   512→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter shows airlines with flight counts\n   513→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   514→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with results from multiple airlines\n   515→- **Action**: User observes the Airlines filter section\n   516→- **Expected**: A list of airline names is shown, each with a checkbox and a count of how many flights that airline has in the results (e.g., \"Delta (12)\", \"United (8)\").\n   517→\n   518→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select specific airline\n   519→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   520→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from Delta, United, and American\n   521→- **Action**: User checks the \"Delta\" checkbox in the Airlines filter\n   522→- **Expected**: Only Delta flights are shown in results. United and American flights are hidden.\n   523→\n   524→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select multiple airlines\n   525→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   526→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from multiple airlines\n   527→- **Action**: User checks \"Delta\" and \"United\"\n   528→- **Expected**: Only Delta and United flights are shown. Other airline flights are hidden.\n   529→\n   530→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider displays histogram\n   531→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   532→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   533→- **Action**: User observes the Price range filter section\n   534→- **Expected**: A price range slider is displayed with min and max handles. Above or within the slider, a histogram shows the distribution of prices across the results. The min and max price labels are shown.\n   535→\n   536→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider filters results\n   537→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   538→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   539→- **Action**: User drags the max price handle to $400\n   540→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $400 or below are displayed. Flights above $400 are hidden. The slider shows the updated max value.\n   541→\n   542→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider — adjust min price\n   543→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   544→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   545→- **Action**: User drags the min price handle to $300\n   546→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $300 or above are displayed. Flights below $300 are hidden.\n   547→\n   548→#### Test: FilterSidebar duration range slider filters results\n   549→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   550→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   551→- **Action**: User adjusts the duration slider to max 6 hours\n   552→- **Expected**: Only flights with duration of 6 hours or less are displayed. Longer flights are hidden.\n   553→\n   554→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — Morning checkbox\n   555→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   556→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   557→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" in the Departure time filter\n   558→- **Expected**: Only flights departing in the morning time window are displayed.\n   559→\n   560→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — multiple time periods\n   561→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   562→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   563→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" and \"Evening\"\n   564→- **Expected**: Flights departing in either morning or evening time windows are displayed. Afternoon and night flights are hidden.\n   565→\n   566→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — arrival time checkboxes\n   567→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   568→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   569→- **Action**: User checks \"Afternoon\" in the arrival time checkbox group\n   570→- **Expected**: Only flights arriving in the afternoon are displayed.\n   571→\n   572→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by dropdown — default \"Best\"\n   573→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   574→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, no sort selection made\n   575→- **Action**: User observes the Sort by dropdown\n   576→- **Expected**: The dropdown shows \"Best\" as the default selected sort option.\n   577→\n   578→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Price (lowest)\n   579→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   580→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flights at different prices\n   581→- **Action**: User selects \"Price (lowest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   582→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the cheapest flight first. Prices increase going down the list.\n   583→\n   584→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Duration (shortest)\n   585→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   586→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   587→- **Action**: User selects \"Duration (shortest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   588→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the shortest flight first. Durations increase going down the list.\n   589→\n   590→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Departure time (earliest)\n   591→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   592→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various departure times\n   593→- **Action**: User selects \"Departure time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   594→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest departure first.\n   595→\n   596→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Arrival time (earliest)\n   597→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   598→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various arrival times\n   599→- **Action**: User selects \"Arrival time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   600→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest arrival first.\n   601→\n   602→#### Test: FilterSidebar combining multiple filters\n   603→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   604→- **Initial state**: Results page with diverse flights\n   605→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\" in Stops, selects \"Delta\" in Airlines, and sets max price to $500\n   606→- **Expected**: Only nonstop Delta flights priced at $500 or below are shown. All three filters are applied simultaneously.\n   607→\n   608→#### Test: FilterSidebar filters can be used repeatedly\n   609→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   610→- **Initial state**: Results page with no filters\n   611→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\", observes filtered results, then unchecks \"Nonstop\" and checks \"1 stop\", then changes sort to \"Price (lowest)\"\n   612→- **Expected**: Each filter change updates results correctly. The filters work properly on repeated use.\n   613→\n   614→### FlightResultCard\n   615→\n   616→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays airline info\n   617→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   618→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with flights\n   619→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   620→- **Expected**: The card shows a colored circle with the airline's initials (airline logo) and the airline name next to it.\n   621→\n   622→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays departure and arrival times\n   623→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   624→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   625→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   626→- **Expected**: The card shows departure time → arrival time (e.g., \"8:00 AM → 4:30 PM\"). If the flight arrives on a different day, a \"+1\" day indicator is shown next to the arrival time.\n   627→\n   628→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays flight duration\n   629→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   630→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   631→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   632→- **Expected**: The card shows the total flight duration in hours and minutes format (e.g., \"5h 30m\").\n   633→\n   634→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays stops and layover info\n   635→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   636→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with a connecting flight\n   637→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card for a connecting flight\n   638→- **Expected**: The card shows the number of stops and layover airport codes (e.g., \"1 stop · DFW\"). A nonstop flight shows \"Nonstop\".\n   639→\n   640→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays price prominently\n   641→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   642→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   643→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   644→- **Expected**: The price is displayed prominently and right-aligned on the card (e.g., \"$342\").\n   645→\n   646→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays CO₂ emissions\n   647→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   648→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   649→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   650→- **Expected**: A CO₂ emissions estimate is shown on the card (e.g., \"130 kg CO₂\").\n   651→\n   652→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand to show details\n   653→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   654→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, flight card is collapsed\n   655→- **Action**: User clicks on a flight result card to expand it\n   656→- **Expected**: The card expands to show a detailed section including: each leg of the journey with departure/arrival times and airports, terminal info, layover duration and airport (for connecting flights), aircraft type, amenities icons (Wi-Fi, power, entertainment), and baggage allowance information.\n   657→\n   658→#### Test: FlightResultCard collapse details\n   659→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   660→- **Initial state**: A flight result card is expanded showing details\n   661→- **Action**: User clicks the card again to collapse it\n   662→- **Expected**: The expanded details section collapses. The card returns to its compact view.\n   663→\n   664→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show leg-by-leg breakdown\n   665→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   666→- **Initial state**: A connecting flight card is expanded\n   667→- **Action**: User examines the expanded details\n   668→- **Expected**: Each leg is shown separately with: departure time and airport (with terminal), arrival time and airport (with terminal), flight number, and duration. Between legs, the layover duration and airport are displayed.\n   669→\n   670→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show amenities icons\n   671→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   672→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   673→- **Action**: User examines the amenities section\n   674→- **Expected**: Icons for available amenities are shown: Wi-Fi icon (if has_wifi), power outlet icon (if has_power), entertainment icon (if has_entertainment). Only available amenities are shown or unavailable ones are visually muted.\n   675→\n   676→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show baggage allowance\n   677→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   678→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   679→- **Action**: User examines the baggage section\n   680→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed in the expanded details.\n   681→\n   682→#### Test: FlightResultCard overnight flight shows +1 day indicator\n   683→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   684→- **Initial state**: Results include an overnight flight (e.g., departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM next day)\n   685→- **Action**: User observes the overnight flight card\n   686→- **Expected**: The arrival time shows a \"+1\" indicator next to it (e.g., \"6:00 AM +1\") to indicate arrival on the next day.\n   687→\n   688→#### Test: FlightResultCard clicking \"Select\" navigates to booking page\n   689→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   690→- **Initial state**: Results page with flight cards, a card is expanded\n   691→- **Action**: User clicks the select/book button on a flight card\n   692→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Flight Details / Booking page with the selected flight's information.\n   693→\n   694→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand and collapse multiple cards\n   695→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   696→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flight cards\n   697→- **Action**: User expands card A, then expands card B, then collapses card A\n   698→- **Expected**: Each card independently expands and collapses. Card B remains expanded when card A is collapsed.\n   699→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015XqURnhAyaFzZdjoANsF8q","session_id":"e83b6a70-0e11-4c8e-bdc4-82e0f5b3de96","uuid":"06523c1f-a998-47df-8ba8-d181b04c22bc"}
